<title>CANADA: Saskatchewan sets C$200 mln 6.125 pct due 2001.</title>
<headline>Saskatchewan sets C$200 mln 6.125 pct due 2001.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The province of Saskatchewan on Thursday set a C$200 million, 6.125 percent bond due, October 10, 2001, said lead manager CIBC Wood Gundy Securities Inc.</p>
<p>The issue was priced at C$99.025 to yield 6.356 percent with a spread of 10 basis points over the Government of Canada 7.0 percent bond due September, 2001.</p>
<p>The new issue will be delivered on October 10.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
